WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.680
Let's make Pinecone woodland friends.

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:08.079
Give a dry pinecone a stable clay base and large paper features to make

3
00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:10.230
an owl, hedgehog or imaginary friend.

4
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.690
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.800
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.425
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:18.805 --> 00:00:22.250
An adult checks cone scales and prepares paper shapes.

8
00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.591
Use paper features rather than small detachable eyes, and keep the sculpture on a

9
00:00:27.591 --> 00:00:28.300
stable base.

10
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:31.023
Step 1.

11
00:00:31.403 --> 00:00:32.993
Make a stable base.

12
00:00:33.373 --> 00:00:37.403
Flatten the clay into a disc about 6 centimetres wide on the card.

13
00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:40.318
Press the wide end of the pinecone into it.

14
00:00:40.698 --> 00:00:45.230
If making a hedgehog, lay the cone sideways and press it gently into the

15
00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:45.553
clay.

16
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:47.313
Grown-up help.

17
00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:50.288
Check the cone and help it sit steadily.

18
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:53.013
Step 2.

19
00:00:53.393 --> 00:00:54.908
Choose the features.

20
00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:59.183
Arrange large paper wings, ears or a face beside the cone.

21
00:00:59.563 --> 00:01:02.888
Draw eyes directly on the paper face with a crayon.

22
00:01:03.268 --> 00:01:06.273
Try the shapes against the cone before attaching.

23
00:01:06.653 --> 00:01:08.033
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:08.413 --> 00:01:11.318
Prepare paper shapes for younger makers.

25
00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:14.178
Step 3.

26
00:01:14.558 --> 00:01:16.353
Fold attachment tabs.

27
00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:20.981
Fold about 1 centimetres at the base of each paper feature to make a

28
00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:21.588
small tab.

29
00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:24.478
Put a loop of paper tape on the tab.

30
00:01:24.858 --> 00:01:27.213
Keep the decorative part clear of the tape.

31
00:01:27.593 --> 00:01:28.973
Grown-up help.

32
00:01:29.353 --> 00:01:31.903
Make tape loops for younger makers.

33
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.483
Step 4.

34
00:01:34.863 --> 00:01:36.598
Give your friend a face.

35
00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:41.208
Press the taped tabs onto broad cone scales, one piece at a time.

36
00:01:41.588 --> 00:01:43.558
Hold gently for a moment.

37
00:01:43.938 --> 00:01:48.633
Add a larger tape loop if a piece falls off; avoid forcing paper between

38
00:01:48.633 --> 00:01:49.303
sharp scales.

39
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:51.063
Grown-up help.

40
00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:54.173
Help secure pieces and check the base.

41
00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:56.842
Step 5.

42
00:01:57.222 --> 00:01:59.387
Make a woodland introduction.

43
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.057
Let the friend sit on the card base.

44
00:02:02.437 --> 00:02:05.112
Give it a name and tell what it likes to do.

45
00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:09.869
Move it by lifting the card, not by pulling on the cone or paper

46
00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:10.182
features.

47
00:02:10.562 --> 00:02:11.942
Grown-up help.

48
00:02:12.322 --> 00:02:14.882
Carry the finished creation if needed.

49
00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:19.249
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

50
00:02:19.629 --> 00:02:23.179
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

51
00:02:23.559 --> 00:02:25.579
Your creation can look different.

52
00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:31.239
Remove paper and tape, reuse the clay and card, and sort the cone appropriately.

53
00:02:31.619 --> 00:02:35.069
Keep dry indoors, away from younger children and pets.

54
00:02:35.449 --> 00:02:36.439
Well done.

55
00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:39.249
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

